Z||000004||PBJ||05-22-2001||09:31 PM||||I had to put a converter on mine because when I bought it, there was a test pipe in its place. I did notice an improvement in performance right away.  I would not take mine back off without correcting back pressures.  The converter I installed is a newer style honeycomb.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||05-22-2001||09:36 PM||||I took mine off and noticed an increase in performance right away. The converter is restrictive and you will make more power without it but it will move the torque band higher. It also sounds better too.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000006||gtsonly||05-22-2001||09:41 PM||||I just finished putting a straight pipe on my 86 gt. I used a 22 inch piece of 2 1/4" pipe and cut the cat off. I have to believe the car is breathing better after looking at the cat and the weight loss has to be good also. The car sounds like a camaro. Nice rumble to it. Sounds like it has more than a V6 in it. A tad louder than stock but well worth the effort to do it. If anyone has any questions for me feel free to ask. No big secret here.<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||14
Z||000007||cadaver||05-22-2001||10:16 PM||||A Camaro? Put it back on||||reg||1
