Z||000009||gtsonly||05-23-2001||08:28 AM||||Not that I like camaro's or anything but it has the sound note of said car. <P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||6
Z||000010||AusFiero||05-23-2001||11:45 AM||||A trick we use down this way is to gut the cat and put a straight pipe through it. That way if a cop or someone checks it over without emmission testing equipment it all looks stock.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||14
Z||000011||cadaver||05-23-2001||11:39 PM||||Is that like a  camaro that has the v6 very similar to the 6 of a fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000012||camaro2fiero||05-24-2001||02:27 AM||||Thats a cool idea AusFiero.||||reg||6
Z||000013||Mach10||05-24-2001||09:37 PM||||I had it done, almost. I had a cherry-bomb welded in place of it (thanks for the idea Ski!!!). The car REALLY wails at high revs. Not ricey, but it just SCREAMS. It has a little less bottom-end on it, but it starts to pick up a lot harder after 4000 or so. At normal driving, it's not much louder than stock, but it rumbles nicely to itself at idle. Put a resonator, not a straight-pipe. Pipe makes it a little harsh for my taste. I've heard it done.||||reg||6
